# @[is: predicate] guard in CaseArm position — supported via eval_structural_pattern_inner.
# The case arm binds the scrutinee to `result`, then the [is: ...] predicate tests [> result 5].
# Scrutinee 10 satisfies [> 10 5], so the "matched" arm fires.
[
  expected: 10
  result: [match 10
    [case [let result] result@[is: [> result 5]] "matched"]
    ...:                                         "no match"]
]
=== out
Dict({"expected": Int(10), "result": String("matched")})
